<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Baillie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1782</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Baillie (died 1782) was a Scottish officer of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> army. In September 1780, at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-mysore-war">Second Anglo-Mysore War</a>, his detachment was surrounded and destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> at Pollilur, one of the Company's heaviest defeats in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Baillie was taken prisoner and died in captivity at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> in 1782.</p></div>
